        mt=1,2,4,51-55,91,102                                     1637 1451   57
           Total, elastic, inelastic and capture                  1637 1451   58
         calculated with casthy code /2/, considering the         1637 1451   59
         competition with the threshold reaction channels.        1637 1451   60
           Optical potential parameters of C.Y.Fu/3/ are adjusted 1637 1451   61
         to reproduce the following experimental data:            1637 1451   62
             mt=1  total -                                        1637 1451   63
             mt=2  elastic cross sections of s-32                 1637 1451   64
             mt=4  inelastic -                                    1637 1451   65
         The spherical optical potential parameters:              1637 1451   66
             V = 38.0      Vso= 5.37  (MeV)                       1637 1451   67
             Ws= 9.13      Wv = 0.0   (MeV)                       1637 1451   68
             r =rso= 1.26  rs = 1.39  (fm)                        1637 1451   69
             a =aso= 0.76  b  = 0.40  (fm)                        1637 1451   70
           mt=102 capture data are normalized to 0.15 mb at 1 MeV 1637 1451   71
         based on s-32 capture cross section.                     1637 1451   72
           The discrete level scheme taken from ref./4/:          1637 1451   73
             no.     energy (MeV)     spin-parity                 1637 1451   74
           (g.s.)      0.0              0   +                     1637 1451   75
              1        3.291            2   +                     1637 1451   76
              2        3.346            0   +                     1637 1451   77
              3        4.192            3   -                     1637 1451   78
              4        4.523            1   +                     1637 1451   79
              5        4.575            2   +                     1637 1451   80
         Continuum levels assumed above 5.0 MeV. The level        1637 1451   81
         density parameters of Asano et al./5/ are used.          1637 1451   82
